Summary of behavioural changes to existing code:

  * Float32 prior distributions are widened to float64 rather than rejected.
  * A warning is emitted when media history is too short for the adstock
    window, which otherwise zero-pads silently.
  * Non-finite variables are excluded from the VIF check rather than aborting
    it.
  * Several input-validation errors now name the offending column, coordinate
    or value.
  * Test-only fixes for protobuf >= 6 and for Python 3.11 mock behaviour.

No change alters the model's statistical specification. Feature requests that
would have done so are declined in TRIAGE.md with reasons.
